  "notes": "`PRODUCT_VERSION` 1.4.3 · `CONTRACT_VERSION` 4.10.0\n\n1.4.3 keeps a new memory from replacing the older one it builds on, and makes sure toryo's background services always find your tools.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- **A memory that refines an older one no longer replaces it.** Both are kept, so the earlier knowledge stays available.\n- **You're told when a memory is rejected.** Before, it could look as if the memory had been saved.\n- **Background services always find your tools and your toryo data**, however they were started.\n- **Commands refuse options that belong to a different command** rather than ignoring them, and asking any command for help shows that command's own help.",
